# English only

This repository is **English-only**. Agents must never write Arabic anywhere in the project.

## Required language

- **All repo files**: English only — docs, comments, commit messages, PR descriptions, code strings, configs, and agent prompts checked into git.
- **Agent chat in this workspace**: English only when discussing or changing project files.
- **User-facing copy in source**: English in `en.ts` and default strings; use the i18n locale files for other languages, not inline Arabic.

## When you find Arabic

1. Translate it to clear English.
2. Do not add new Arabic text “for the user’s convenience.”
3. Do not mix Arabic and English in the same file.

## Examples

```markdown
<!-- BAD -->
# [Arabic heading — not allowed]

<!-- GOOD -->
# Development guide
```

```typescript
// BAD — Arabic string literal
const label = "<Arabic text>";

// GOOD
const label = "Save"; // or use t('save') from i18n
```

## Verification

Run `node scripts/check-english-only.mjs` before pushing. CI runs this as part of `pnpm verify`.
